# Machine ingress owner: services/control/internal/platform/config/machine_server.go.
# Merge selected keys into the existing protected0600 single-link serve --env-file.
# Base YAML must already contain an independently valid complete machine_server group.
# Omission has no defaults; environment values never create, enable or unset the group.
# No ambient environment, shell expansion, source rebuild or live reload is used.
# Native listener configuration is this increment; Compose/Helm/projection and dedicated
# operator/agent/gateway examples require their separate declared deployment increment.

# Owner machine_server.listen_address; required string canonical host:port, port1..65535.
# No default or units beyond numeric TCP port; bracket IPv6. Bind differs from server.listen_address.
# Public nonsecret bind, separate from advertised origin; wildcard0.0.0.0/[::] is bind-only.
# Explicit protected env-file overrides valid YAML; restart rebinds both sockets, refusing conflicts.
PROJECT_ONE_MACHINE_LISTEN_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1:9443

# Owner machine_server.origin; required canonical HTTPS origin string, no default or plaintext mode.
# No path/query/fragment/userinfo; lowercase DNS/localhost, exact IPv4 or bracketed IPv6.
# Omit default443; nondefault numeric ports1..65535 are explicit. Distinct from both browser origins.
# Public binding, no secret contents. Env-file overrides valid YAML; restart and reconcile/fence old
# agent/gateway identities and uncertain spools before issuing a new explicit identity for this origin.
PROJECT_ONE_MACHINE_ORIGIN=https://machine.example.invalid:9443

# Owner machine_server.tls_certificate_file; required canonical absolute file-reference string.
# No default; distinct from the key. Reference only, never PEM or private bytes in this env file.
# Startup bounds the actual single-link regular input to1MiB and checks pair/validity/machine SAN.
# Public readable0444/0644 is allowed; actual owner/group and parent/file facts must remain stable.
# Explicit env-file overrides valid YAML; restart required. Normal client CA/name verification remains.
PROJECT_ONE_MACHINE_TLS_CERTIFICATE_FILE=/run/projectone/private/machine-certificate.pem

# Owner machine_server.tls_private_key_file; required canonical absolute protected reference string.
# No default; distinct from the certificate. Secret reference only; never put key contents here.
# Actual OS-readable0400/0600 single-link regular file, no group/other permissions, at most1MiB;
# pinned parent/descriptor/path checks reject links, special files, replacement and restored-mtime edits.
# Explicit env-file overrides valid YAML; restart required. No TLS downgrade or verification bypass.
PROJECT_ONE_MACHINE_TLS_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE=/run/projectone/private/machine-key.pem
